/-! # Part X. `YangMills.StrongCoupling.FibreReduction`: `hFibre` reduced to a coarse-constrained cube bound (new; uses Parts I–IV, VI and VII) -/

/-!
# The fibre bound `hFibre` reduced to a coarse-constrained cube bound

## (a) Formal target

`hFibre` of `CubeSplitInterface` (row S5) asks for `λ` with `λ ‖u‖² ≤ ⟪u, D u⟫` whenever `Π u = 0`,
where `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)` is the cube-resampling generator. This module reduces `hFibre`, for the
finite-volume Wilson model of `WilsonSU2Inputs` (straight two-link blocking, `Π = J J*`), to a lower
bound for the *coarse-constrained* generator `∑ₓ wₓ (I − P'ₓ)` on `ker Π`. Here
`P'ₓ = E_μ[· | links outside Vₓ ∖ Sk]`, and `Sk` is the skeleton: the fine links used by the blocking.
It also proves an abstract Dobrushin-type lower bound for such generators.

## (b) What is proved

* Abstract, for orthogonal projections (`SchurSplit.OrthProj`) and `CubeSplit.cubeGen`:
  - `norm_sub_le_of_le`: enlarging the range decreases `‖u − P u‖`;
  - `proj_comp_eq_of_le`: `ran Π ⊆ ran P'` gives `Π P' = Π`;
  - `inner_cubeGen_eq`: `⟪u, cubeGen w P u⟫ = ∑ₓ wₓ ‖u − Pₓ u‖²`;
  - `fibre_of_constrained` (and `fibre_of_constrained_gen`, the same with the bound stated for
    `cubeGen w P'`): if `ran Pₓ ⊆ ran P'ₓ ⊇ ran Π` and `wₓ ≥ 0`, a bound
    `λ ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ₓ wₓ ‖u − P'ₓ u‖²` on `ker Π` gives `hFibre` for `cubeGen w P`.
  - `norm_apply_le_of_pow_decay`: log-convexity. For symmetric `T`, `‖Tⁿ g‖ ≤ C θⁿ` for all `n`
    gives `‖T g‖ ≤ θ ‖g‖`.
  - `dobrushin_gap`: `δᵢ(Pᵢ f) = 0`, `δⱼ(Pᵢ f) ≤ δⱼ f + C i j δᵢ f`, row sums `≤ r` and
    `‖f‖ ≤ K ∑ⱼ δⱼ f` on an invariant subspace give `∑ᵢ ‖f − Pᵢ f‖² ≥ (1 − r) ‖f‖²`.
  - `fibre_of_dobrushin`: the two combined give `hFibre` with `λ = w_min (1 − r)`.
* Wilson, for any finite oriented lattice and blocking (namespace `WilsonCube` objects):
  - `extSigma_anti`;
  - `blockMap_measurable_extSigma`: `σ(c) ≤ 𝓔(V)` when `V` avoids the skeleton;
  - `extSigma_diff_skel_eq`: if no coarse link has both of its fine links in `V`, then
    `𝓔(V ∖ Sk) = 𝓔(V) ⊔ σ(c)`. So `P'ₓ` is exactly the conditional expectation given the
    exterior of `Vₓ` and the coarse field;
  - `wilsonP_fixes_wilsonP` and `wilsonP_fixes_Pi`: `P'ₓ` fixes `ran Pₓ` and `ran Π`;
  - `wilsonPj`: `Pₓ` bundled as a `SchurSplit.OrthProj`;
  - `hFibre_of_constrained` and `hFibre_of_constrained_gen`.
* SU(2) on `(ℤ/2Mℤ)⁴`, every `M ≥ 1`, every real `β`, side-2 interior cubes `cube2 M z`:
  - `cube2_not_both`: no cube contains both fine links of a coarse link;
  - `cube2_meets_skel`: every cube contains a skeleton link in every direction;
  - `su2_hFibre_of_constrained` and `su2_gap_of_constrained`. The second is
    `CubeSplitInputs.gap_of_residual` for `su2_inputs` with `hFibre` replaced by the constrained
    bound `hcons`. The abbreviations `su2J`, `su2P`, `su2Pi`, `su2Jt`, `su2D`, `su2Dc` name the
    objects of `su2_inputs`.
* Closed applications for the explicit model of Part VII of this file (`M = 2`, `β = 1`):
  - `su2_model_cubeLinks_eq`: its cubes are `cube2 2 x`;
  - `su2_model_constrained_closed`: the constrained projections fix `ran Pₓ` and `ran Π`, and the
    cubes satisfy the two geometric facts, with no hypotheses;
  - `su2_model_hFibre_of_constrained`: `hcons` is stated for the constrained generator
    `cubeGen cubeW (P_{Vₓ ∖ Sk})`. No sum over the 256 cubes is written out.

## (c) Hypotheses that remain open

`hcons`, the constrained Poincaré bound `λ ‖u‖² ≤ ∑ₓ wₓ ‖u − P'ₓ u‖²` on `ker Π`, is not proved for
the Wilson measure. It is the only analytic input of `su2_hFibre_of_constrained`. `hResidual` (S6) and
`hCoarseGap` (S7) remain open, and nothing is uniform in the spacing, the volume or the boundary.
The Dobrushin hypotheses of `dobrushin_gap` are not verified for any Wilson heat bath here.
The finite-volume (R1) and strong-coupling (R2) measure theory of the accompanying research notes is not formalised.

## (d) Axioms and checks

Every declaration depends only on `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` (module axiom
audit). The part contains no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom` declarations, `native_decide` or
`implemented_by`. It uses Parts I–IV, VI and VII of this file.

## (e) Scope

This is not a proof of a mass gap and proves no gap for the Wilson measure. It proves an exact
reduction of `hFibre` to a constrained bound, and an abstract criterion for such bounds.
-/

